:: The Supplier [event main_quest] {"position":"5950,500","size":"100,100"}
/* Quest "The Supplier" (main_supplier), STAGE1_PROPOSAL.md 4.12, first half. The last family option, built with <<Offer>>
   (Family offers in Define Quests). Since the diner incident my reading says the right compounds would fix what the Veil
   does to some people. $supplier.callName has them; the name came from $boss.callName (the Boss line, 7.2, not built yet).
   He owns $club. On the phone he names his price: $20,000 up front, which is more than the account holds by design, and
   mentions that cash isn't the only currency his club accepts. Offering them is my idea.
     plain    pay $20,000 from the account (+$2,500 for every stall); usually locked
     plain    take an advance from $boss.callName (setup.addDebt: the money now, $2,500 every Monday for ten weeks)
     family   both of them, level 3 (Handed over), for one evening at his club; locked until both lines have reached
              their optional quests (mom_lastNight, sister_rehearsal)
     stall    think about it: it comes back in a few days, and the price goes up
   Sets $flags.supplierOffered (true: they go, Rehearsal and The Last Night play; false: I pay). */
<<silent>>
	<<SetBackground $locations[14].img>>
	<<set _suStalls to setup.offerStalls("main_supplier")>>
	<<set _suPrice to 20000 + 2500 * _suStalls>>
	<<set _suLock to ((setup.questReached("mom_lastNight") and setup.questReached("sister_rehearsal")) ? "" : "They aren't there yet")>>
<</silent>>
<<if _suStalls == 0>>
Since the night at $diner.name I've read everything I could find: papers, forums, and a used textbook on neurochemistry that I've annotated in three colors by now. As far as I can tell, the Veil doesn't create anything, it amplifies. In most people that comes out as calm, but in a few, the wrong few, it's whatever they were already carrying, only sharper. If I've understood it right, the fix isn't in the device at all. It's in the people in the room, and in a handful of compounds you can't buy in a pharmacy.

$boss.callName gave me the name over a whiskey he didn't offer me: a man who sells to people who don't ask questions, and who owns a club downtown called $club.name.

I call the number at two.
<<else>>
I call $supplier.callName back. He picks up on the first ring this time, and he sounds amused.
<</if>>

/* MEDIA: images/events/the_supplier/phone.jpg | My desk in the afternoon light, the phone to my ear, an annotated chemistry textbook open beside the keyboard */

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $supplier, text: "$player.name. $boss.callName said you'd call, and he said you were young, although I think he undersold it." },
{ who: $player, text: "He said you might be able to get me what I need." },
{ who: $supplier, text: "I can get anybody what they need. What people really call me about is what it costs." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

He has a soft, unhurried voice, the voice of a man who has never once in his life had to raise it. I tell him what I need in the vaguest words I can find, and trip over one of the names, and he doesn't need any more than that. It sounds like he's heard the list before.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $supplier, text: "That's not a small order. And it comes with discretion, which is always the expensive part." },
{ who: $supplier, text: "Twenty thousand, up front. Cash or wire, whichever you prefer." },
{ text: "He says it like a man reading a menu." },
{ who: $supplier, text: "Of course, money isn't the only thing I accept. I run a club, as I'm sure you know, and my members are particular people. They pay for the atmosphere, for good company, for the right faces at the right tables." },
{ who: $supplier, text: "A man who could bring me an evening of that would find me very flexible on price." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

He doesn't say anything else. Maybe he's heard about the rooftop, or about $mom.callName on the sixth floor, or maybe he's just a man who has made this offer before and knows how it lands. Either way he waits, breathing softly on the line, while I look at the company account on my screen. <<if _suStalls > 0>>Since my last call, his price has gone up to $<<= _suPrice.toLocaleString("en-US")>>.<</if>>

<<Offer>>
<<plain "Pay him" `"-$" + _suPrice.toLocaleString("en-US") + " up front"` _suPrice>>
<<silently>>
<<set $flags.supplierOffered to false>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "I'll wire it today." },
{ who: $supplier, text: "Wonderful. Tomorrow night, then, at ten. Come to $club.name, ask for me at the door, and come alone." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

I wire it. The account looks very empty afterwards, emptier than it has looked since the broom closet.

<<NextQuest $player>>
<<ReturnFromEvent>>

<<plain `"Borrow it from " + $boss.callName` "the money now, $2,500 every Monday for ten weeks">>
<<silently>>
<<set $flags.supplierOffered to false>>
<<run setup.addDebt("boss_advance", "Advance from " + $boss.callName, _suPrice, 2500, 10)>>
<<run setup.spend(_suPrice, "The supplier")>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "Okay. Give me an hour to get the money together." },
{ who: $supplier, text: "Take two. Tomorrow night, $club.name, ten o'clock. Come alone." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

I call $boss.callName. He lets it ring five times before he picks up, so I'll know he can. When I tell him how much and what for, he laughs, a long, wet, delighted laugh, and says of course, kid, of course, what are friends for, and names his terms, which are worse than a bank's and better than nothing. The money is in the account in twenty minutes. Twenty-one minutes later it's gone again.

Every Monday for ten weeks I'll be paying the man who used to yell at $mom.callName in front of the whole sixth floor. I'm pretty sure he knows exactly how that feels for me, and that it's half of why he said yes.

<<UpdateStat "+" "Corruption" 1>>
<<NextQuest $player>>
<<ReturnFromEvent>>

<<family `[$mom, $sister]` 3 `"Offer him an evening with " + $mom.callName + " and " + $sister.callName` "the price, gone" _suLock>>
<<silently>>
<<set $flags.supplierOffered to true>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "What if I brought you two hostesses for an evening at your club? Really good ones." },
{ text: "There's a pause on the line, and for the first time his voice isn't quite as soft when he answers." },
{ who: $supplier, text: "Two of them. Well, that is a very generous offer, $player.name." },
{ who: $supplier, text: "The day after tomorrow, then, at ten o'clock. You can drive them yourself, though you'll wait outside, of course. The club is for members only." },
{ who: $player, text: "Of course." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

He hangs up. I sit there for a while with the phone in my hand and the account balance on the screen, untouched.

I haven't told either of them yet, and neither of them knows the other one is going. Tomorrow evening I'll take $sister.callName into the meeting room and rehearse it with her, and I'll tell $mom.callName what to wear, and I'm hoping neither of them asks why.

<<UpdateStat "+" "Corruption" 4>>
<<NextQuest $player>>
<<ReturnFromEvent>>

<<stall "Think it over" "main_supplier" "his price will go up">>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "I need to think about it for a few days." },
{ who: $supplier, text: "Think as long as you like. My prices are patient. They just get a little bigger while they wait." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<ReturnFromEvent>>
<</Offer>>
